//****************************************************************************
// $Module type: Class Package
// $Module name: cFTActionBarHost
// $Author     : Nils Svedmyr, RDC Tools International, <mailto:support@rdctools.com>
// Web-site    : http://www.rdctools.com
// Created     : 2026-10-14
//
// Description : A dialog's action menu: a small FT host, at the dialog's top right, holding a cFTWebActionBar
//               and a cWebMenuGroup of menu items - as a web program's header holds its action bar and a web
//               view declares its oActionGroup; the items act on the grid, field or host the focus came from.
//
// This code is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
// without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
//****************************************************************************
Use cFTLocalWebControlHost.pkg
Use cDbLocalWebControlHost.pkg     // to tell a data-aware host from a plain one (ActionTarget)
Use cWebActionBar.pkg
Use cFTWebActionBar.pkg     // the bar the dialog declares in the host
Use cWebMenuGroup.pkg
Use cFTWebMenuItem.pkg
Use cFTWebMenuNew.pkg       // New, Save and Delete on the object the focus came from
Use cFTWebMenuSave.pkg
Use cFTWebMenuDelete.pkg

/* A DIALOG'S ACTION MENU (Nils 2026-10-14) - the FT way of a web view's actions. A web view declares them in a
   cWebMenuGroup (DataFlex's FlexTron sample ZoomInventory.wo: oActionGroup with Save and Edit), and the web
   program's action bar - a cWebActionBar in its header - shows them. Here this host is the header, and the
   dialog declares both in it - the bar (cFTWebActionBar, with the FT defaults) and the group:

       Object oActions is a cFTActionBarHost
           Set Location to 2 250
           Set Size to 26 170
           Set peAnchors to anTopRight

           Object oActionBar is a cFTWebActionBar
           End_Object

           Object oActionGroup is a cWebMenuGroup
               Object oNew_itm is a cFTWebMenuNew
               End_Object

               Object oSave_itm is a cFTWebMenuSave
               End_Object

               Object oDelete_itm is a cFTWebMenuDelete
               End_Object
           End_Object
       End_Object

   The group and the bar find each other by name - psGroupName "MainActions", the framework's default on both -
   on the host's own page. Each host is a page of its own, so the group is declared in this host; a dialog has
   one of them. Whether an item shows and whether it can be clicked is the framework's: pbRender and pbEnabled of
   the item, with WebSet once the page is up (FTHostPageIsUp). An item of the dialog's own is a cFTWebMenuItem
   with its work in OnItemClick.

   THE ITEMS ACT WHERE THE USER IS (Nils 2026-10-14: "usually achieved with the Focus function"). DataFlex's own
   toolbar items send Request_Save, Request_Clear and Request_Delete to the object with the focus (DEOFocus) - a
   CodeJock toolbar never takes the focus. A click on this bar does: the WebView2 control takes it, through
   DataFlex's own focus change (Mouse_Change_Focus, then Entering). So Entering, below, remembers the object the
   focus comes from, before it moves, and ActionTarget hands it to the items: a CodeJock grid, a Windows field, or
   a data-aware FT host - which carries a request out on its own data dictionary (cDbLocalWebControlHost is a
   data-entry client). An object without a data dictionary - a button bar - is no target: an item does nothing
   then.

   THE BAR (cFTWebActionBar): right-aligned, with captions (an action bar hides them by default), the items in
   the FT buttons' look (ftcontrols.css) with their glyph classes (ftglyphs.css). The dialog declares it - this
   class builds nothing - so the Studio's Designer draws the bar with the group's items, as the program does. ITS HEIGHT: a row of FT buttons is 33 px with
   its margins, and a host pads its content by 4 px above and below - 26 units hold it at 100 % and above, as
   the FT dialogs' button bars. Its width: the buttons' (76 px at least, 6 px apart) and 4 px; an item that does
   not fit is cut off, not moved to a More list. */
{ DesignerClass=cDTWebControlHost }
{ DesignerJSClass=df.WebApp }
{ OverrideProperty=psCSSClass InitialValue="FtHost" }
Class cFTActionBarHost is a cFTLocalWebControlHost

    Procedure Construct_Object
        Forward Send Construct_Object

        // The object the focus came from when it entered this host - the one the items act on (ActionTarget).
        { Visibility=Private }
        Property Handle phoActionFocus 0
    End_Procedure

    // The focus comes here - by a click on the bar, or by Tab. Before it moves, Focus is the object it comes from.
    { Visibility=Private }
    Procedure Entering Returns Integer
        Handle hoFocus
        Integer iRetVal

        Move (Focus(Desktop)) to hoFocus
        Forward Get msg_Entering to iRetVal
        If ((iRetVal = 0) and (hoFocus > Desktop) and (hoFocus <> Self)) ;
            Set phoActionFocus to hoFocus
        Procedure_Return iRetVal
    End_Procedure

    /* The object the menu's items act on: the one the focus came from, when it is a data-entry object - a grid, a
       field, a data-aware host; 0 when it is not. A web host that is not data-aware - a button bar - holds no
       record. Any other object is a data-entry object when it has a data dictionary (Server), asked with
       delegation off, so an object without one answers 0 rather than handing the question to its panel - the
       way DataFlex's Is_Function asks (Dfpanel.pkg). */
    Function ActionTarget Returns Handle
        Handle hoTarget hoServer
        Integer iMode
        Get phoActionFocus to hoTarget
        If (hoTarget = 0) ;
            Function_Return 0
        If (IsObjectOfClass(hoTarget, RefClass(cLocalWebControlHost)) and not(IsObjectOfClass(hoTarget, RefClass(cDbLocalWebControlHost)))) ;
            Function_Return 0
        Get Delegation_Mode of hoTarget to iMode
        Set Delegation_Mode of hoTarget to No_Delegate_Or_Error
        Get Server of hoTarget to hoServer
        Set Delegation_Mode of hoTarget to iMode
        If (hoServer = 0) ;
            Function_Return 0
        Function_Return hoTarget
    End_Function

End_Class
